# Echo out - the leaving track trails off into a real, fading echo.
#
# Used to be a top-end lift dressed up in the name: an echo whose tail cannot be
# faded is a tail that never stops, which is worse than none, so `echo` was a
# switch, not a knob. It is a lane now - `aecho`'s feedback riding up as the gain
# rides down - so what plays out is an actual, decaying series of repeats instead of
# a fixed EQ shape that only ever sounds like more top end.

name    Echo out
note    the leaving track trails off into a real echo
align   free
tempo   free
power   constant

lane out gain
    at 0.0    1.0    power-down
    at 1.0    0.0    hold

lane in gain
    at 0.0    0.0    power-up
    at 1.0    1.0    hold

lane out echo
    at 0.0    0.0     linear
    at 0.8    0.55    smooth
    at 1.0    0.55    hold
